From eb4e40f9f5b9ce5a92ee8e4b6b6d758fbac5fba1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "live-speech-filter (local)" <local@live-speech-filter.invalid>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 09:20:26 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] companion-mode

Broadcast mode choice: OBS streams itself, or the Douyin companion route
(OBS virtual camera for the picture, OBS audio monitoring into VB-CABLE
for the censored sound). The companion mode starts the virtual camera,
points monitoring at CABLE Input, monitors the sources active in the
program (restored when they leave or the mode is turned off), warns when
a Windows default playback role is the cable (with a fix via
IPolicyConfig), when the virtual camera does not output the program, and
when the companion app's own audio mix (webcast_mate audioStore.json)
captures anything besides CABLE Output. Turning the mode on shows a
checklist for the companion side. The settings dialog now scrolls so the
buttons stay reachable.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
